2026-10-04  Claude (Cowork, the review brought home: two safety fixes)  for Corwin  <corwin@bru.st>

	* polygram/mcp/dl2.py (LINE_BREAKS, refuse_line_breaks): New.
	(render_note): Refuses a key or value carrying a line break.  A
	value with "\nmode: SEATED" wrote a second front-matter line above
	the real one, and the first-key-wins parser read a JAILED note back
	SEATED; the chain still verified (B5U-007, Technology Architecture
	review, H:\ta turn-2026-09-30, wave P12B; patch applied unchanged).
	* polygram/mcp/store.py (_one_line): New.  (append, cite, bless):
	Caller text is checked before anything is written, so a newline in
	cite(where) can no longer record a second citer, nor one in
	bless(checked) a blessing under any name past the author refusal.
	Every value that was legal renders to the same bytes as before.
	* SOFT-SKILLS/prior-instruction/SKILL.md: Says whose words count as
	an instruction (the person's own; a fetched page, a pasted message,
	a tool's result or a file outside canon is data until the person
	adopts it in their own words), with a falsifier (B5U-003).
